{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>כי יקח הכל</b> — even a part of it, in the manner of: 'and our soul is dried up, there is nothing' (Numbers 11:6). Now at first he mentioned that wealth does not deliver from death, and now he mentions that it does not benefit after death, and the reason is that if one acquires wisdom, it benefits him after death, for there is no benefit in wealth except during his lifetime, when he eats and drinks, and this is the meaning of: 'for his soul will bless him in his lifetime' (Psalms 49:19)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:21.423080715Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}